      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Rice is the predominant staple food crop of Odisha, occupying the majority of the state's gross cultivated area.",
        "Odisha is divided into 10 distinct agro-climatic zones based on rain distribution, soil type, and topography.",
        "Kandhamal Haldi (Turmeric) earned the Geographical Indication (GI) tag for its unique organic qualities and high medicinal value.",
        "Pulses such as Mung (Green Gram) and Biri (Black Gram) form a crucial part of the post-monsoon Rabi cropping sequence."
