    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vt074d5",
      "content": "Agriculture is the primary occupation of ~65% of Odisha's population. Paddy (rice) is the most important food crop. The state has three main cropping seasons: Kharif (Biali/Sarada), Rabi, and Zaid (Summer). Odisha is known as the 'Rice Bowl of the East'."
    },
